# FPGA-Image-Enhancement

## Quantization-Aware Residual CNN for FPGA-Based Image Enhancement

FPGA-accelerated image enhancement using Residual CNNs, INT8 quantization, and Vitis AI deployment.

This project focuses on building a fast and hardware-efficient image restoration pipeline capable of enhancing degraded images while maintaining high inference performance on FPGA platforms.

---

## ✨ Features

- Residual CNN image enhancement
- INT8 quantization workflow
- FPGA-accelerated inference
- Vitis AI deployment pipeline
- `.xmodel` generation support
- PSNR / SSIM evaluation
- Docker-based environment
- Hardware benchmarking

---

## 🚀 Project Overview

Modern image enhancement models achieve strong results on GPUs but are often difficult to deploy efficiently on edge hardware.

This project combines:

- Deep learning image restoration
- FPGA hardware acceleration
- Quantization-aware optimization
- Efficient deployment workflows

The system is designed to restore images affected by:

- Noise
- Blur
- Low-light degradation
- Real-world image artifacts

while achieving fast and efficient inference on FPGA hardware.

---

## 🧠 Deployment Pipeline

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Residual CNN Training
   ↓
Quantization-Aware Optimization
   ↓
INT8 XModel Generation
   ↓
DPU Compilation
   ↓
FPGA Inference
   ↓
Enhanced Output
```

---

## 🛠 Technology Stack

| Area | Technology |
|------|-------------|
| Deep Learning | PyTorch |
| Deployment Framework | Vitis AI |
| Hardware Platform | Xilinx FPGA |
| Quantization | INT8 |
| Runtime | DPU Execution |
| Environment | Docker |
| Language | Python 3.10 |

---

## ⚡ Hardware Platform

Validated on:

- Xilinx ZCU104 FPGA Board
- Vitis AI Runtime Environment
- DPU-Based Hardware Acceleration

